\details{
Spherical PCA is a robust alternative to classical PCA that:
\enumerate{
\item Centers data using spatial median (\code{\link{spat}})
\item Projects each observation onto unit sphere: yᵢ = (xᵢ - center) / ||xᵢ - center||
\item Computes covariance of spherical data
\item Obtains eigenvectors from spherical covariance
\item Computes robust eigenvalues using \code{var.fun} on projected scores
}

This approach downweights extreme observations and provides resistance to outliers.
The method can handle heavy-tailed distributions better than classical PCA.

This function provides access to the rrcov package's implementation of spherical PCA.
The rrcov implementation may offer additional features and optimizations compared to
the basic \code{\link{spca}} function.

\strong{Note}: Requires the rrcov package to be installed.
}
